"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible: 4.5, 4.5.1, 4.6, 4.6.1\n- Not reproducible: 4.4.1\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.6.1.stable (14d19694e) - Arch Linux #1 SMP PREEMPT_DYNAMIC Mon, 09 Feb 2026 17:16:33 +0000 on X11 - X11 display driver, Single-window, 2 monitors - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3060 Ti (nvidia; 590.48.01) - 13th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i5-13400F (16 threads) - 15.37 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f15fdcd8-5596-46c8-8006-99ca542de9e4\n\nI can't add entries to a `Dictionary` member of a remote `Node`. This works fine before 4.5.\n\nThe core problem is that the type switch does not work. Selecting a type produces this error:\n\n```\nTried to change the type of a dict key or value, but nothing was selected.\n```\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nAdd a dictionary in a node's script, e.g.,:\n\n```\n@export var foo: Dictionary\n```\n\n- Run the scene\n- Switch to the Remote scene tree and select that node\n- Inspect the `foo` member of that node\n    - Trying to change any of the types produces an error\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[test-4.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/25525129/test-4.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url"